## 📖 What Is This

`ai-short-drama` is a Codex Skill built for **batch production of AI vertical short dramas / motion comics**. Its input is deliberately minimal — one `剧本.md` per episode that follows the format contract, plus that episode's five-view character sheets and scene boards. Its output is equally explicit — a single **1088×1920, 24fps vertical MP4 with native character speech**.

This project does not try to be a universal video generator. Its boundary is hard-coded in SKILL.md: **from an existing script and assets to a finished MP4**. Pure text writing is out of scope — that belongs to the `story-*` skills. What it solves is the most tedious, most repetitive, and most fragile part of the production chain: the part where episode 47's third scene ends up with different lighting than episode 12, and the whole series quietly falls apart. **It takes what is already finalized and renders it, stably, in batches.**

The project landed its first v1 commit on **October 22, 2026**, followed by several iterations — deployment doc fixes and a long-shot render timeout raised from the default to 3 hours. The commit rhythm suggests a tool grown out of real production needs, not a framework written first and looking for a use case later.

