## 🖼️ Asset Requirements: Five-View Sheets and Scene Boards

Five-view character sheet = **full body + front + left profile + right profile + back**. SKILL.md puts this in the iron rules for a reason: "to keep the character from deforming." H3's reference-to-video mode relies on multi-angle reference images to constrain character consistency across shots. Miss one angle and you give the model one more degree of freedom — which it usually spends on "the face changed" or "the clothes are the wrong color."

The scene board is the spatial baseline for each scene. Shot planning sends the five-view sheets and scene board into H3 as dual reference images, so the board's composition, lighting, and color tone directly influence the final frame's mood.

